  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineId addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is appropriate.\n\n- **Placement:** The citation sits on an explicit function with a body. It carries fenced commentary, which is the form `habeas:coverage` requires for a per-function exception.\n- **The reason is substantive:** `node_path` is a required `Domain` trait method on a test-only fixture. The fixture never needs it to be executed.\n- **The reason agrees with the source:**\n  - The only non-test caller of `Domain::node_path` in the crate is `graph.rs#fn[edge_fingerprint]`. It calls `node_path` once per edge target.\n  - `edge_fingerprint` is reached through `dependencies_are_current` for `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`.\n  - The sibling fixture method `outgoing_edges` in `Project`'s `Domain` impl always returns an empty vector. Its own commentary says this source-only fixture has no graph edges. So the per-target closure never runs for `Project`.\n  - The fixture's `source_node` returns `String` ids that tests record directly, and `node_content` is keyed by those ids. Neither uses `node_path`.\n  - The other `node_path` call sites are in other domains' tests: `validation_tests.rs` `ReviewDomain`, and the `Memory` and `TestDomain` fixtures. This is consistent with the claim that other tests use other domains.\n- **Not verified:** I did not read the stable-path or filesystem-storage tests. I confirmed only that no `Project` code path calls `node_path`.\n- **No gap:** No claim in the commentary contradicts the source.",
